  "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $y.$ First, we solve for $y$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}x-2y=2\\sqrt{3}\\,\u27f9\\,y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $y$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2})}^{2} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3(x-2)^{2}}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+4}{4}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}-12x+12}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+16}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+4 & =z+5 \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}-2x-1 \\\\ z & =({x}^{2}-2x+1)-2 \\\\ z & ={(x-1)}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vertex of the projection onto $xz$-plane is $(1,-2).$",
